{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 698df2d0cd3a53ac38c2cb1147a27904d08c5084. Primary 3e995be5 was my FIRST direct FULL read: 46,782 bytes, 705 LF, SHA256 c03526daa294638c6821e7c42dca7d330b69a5c84c1dd528b1d3bdb86938a5e8, eleven contiguous bounded spans through EOF. Three parallel reports were subsequently read FULL. Design review only; no implementation, gate or hosted witness claimed.\n\nP2 — Select revision before handling every HTTP method (§3.4). With a valid November session S, GET /mcp or DELETE /mcp carrying the agent bearer, MCP-Protocol-Version:2026-07-28 and Mcp-Session-Id:S can enter the stated legacy branch: classification expressly covers POST only, the legacy branch accepts either supported header, and modern 405 is limited to requests without a session ID. GET can open the legacy stream; DELETE can end S despite the explicit July revision. Define one method/version matrix: explicit July GET/DELETE returns 405 without opening, consulting or deleting a legacy session; explicit November applies legacy session rules; missing version uses the known session's negotiated context where applicable. Distinguish explicit November without the required session (400) from modern GET/DELETE (405). Add H8 cases with valid and unknown legacy IDs, no stream/no deletion, and S still usable afterward. Keep exactly the commissioned November and July revisions. This is a combined-rules inference, corroborated by official SDK hybrid-mode guidance, not an authentication-bypass claim or a claim that the modern-only server sentence alone governs every hybrid request: https://csharp.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/v2/api/ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore.HttpServerSessionMode.html\n\nArchitecture — Earlier custody blockers are addressed prospectively: each actual send/resubmit/repeat step rearms completion capacity, used and reserved accounting includes retained history, control answers/tombstones reserve before allocation/enrolment, and physical write failure remains recoverable unknown rather than invented immediate success. Authority-before-effects, original mapping/seed/envelope handoff, persisted listed and volatile per-stream notified are retained. The shared HTTP module is the appropriate place for the remaining matrix. H1–H8 and native/hosted implementation still must prove the design.\n\nSecurity — Control origin/full membership/incarnation/action/agent/body/op binding, current authority recheck, original object recovery and atomic bearer/session invalidation are coherent. The secret-residence and old told wording now agree with native history. The remaining cross-era session effects require correction. No new control/custody P1/P2 found; no executed security assurance claimed.\n\nSimplification — Retain the two commissioned revisions and one method/version matrix, without aliases or transport inference from session-header presence. Preserve all original Stage2 scope and later OAuth, reads/resources/prompts/export and parity obligations.\n\nImplementation precision, not additional forced design rounds: settle at full must consume its existing outstanding reservation; a receipt readback must not require fresh send admission space. H6's same-object harness quota increase is coherent; retiring another agent cannot free this object's nondeleting quota. Account net serialized row/chunk/index growth and reserve within the 64MiB identity limit before dispatch. Anchor stored-answer expiry to the original operation's recorded deadline, retain non-reuse tombstones/pending identities, and state the fallback when a full control budget also prevents a new retirement operation (reserved emergency retirement capacity or explicitly qualified native-admin/operator recovery). These criteria preserve original custody rather than silently replacing an operation.\n\nCoverage limits: selected native support inherited only after exact equality with my earlier coverage; whole runtime bodies remain PARTIAL where previously partial. Peer official references are selected excerpts, not whole-page reads. No Source edits, executable generated-artifact interpretation, package installs, runtime/tests/gate, browser/provider/private proof or credential access in this review. Source acceptance and actual delivery remain separate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3e995be52ee457d17635dc64355315c9078c8fcd","binding":"assigned","head":"698df2d0cd3a53ac38c2cb1147a27904d08c5084","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:593c22b034f0d7802382822b7480beb68271fe8a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:705999cfd6bcb95dfac0f52bd180fd0df3511439\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5ef601d2e42f292f28a0138e9f1f901bc90f573","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}